	At the risk of being zapped with a wand of fire again....

	The birds eye view that Nethack gives the player and the
	fact that you can see and attack every monster in a lighted
	area around you (in all directions) is somewhat "unrealistic"
	(whatever that means in the context of NH). An interesting
        addition to the game might be the concept of the player and 
	the monsters "facing" a specific direction. The player
	would then only be able so see and attack monsters that are
	in front (say 45 degrees wide) of him/her. Monsters
	could sneak up on you, but then you could also sneak up on
	them. Of course other things might give them away, like
	sound. And certain objects/attained attributes might
	allow you to see a greater (perhaps 360 degree) range,
	certain helmets for instance. Also some weapons might
	allow you to attack a say 180 (or more) degree range.
	This would make the fighting (particularly hand to hand)
	much more interesting. Of course the real problem with
	implementing this (the game can always be tuned if things
	like this make it too hard) is how to represent the
	direction that the player (and all the monsters) are
	facing given the character set of typical "dumb" terminal.

	While I'm at it here are a few more...

	1)Enhance the use of smell in the game. Every monster and the
	  player have a track of the last X places they have occupied
	  on the level. Some monsters can (and do) track the player.
	  How about the player being able to smell certain monsters
	  (maybe orcs stink!!) or even a new type of pet, a blood
	  hound, useful for tracking down nymphs.

	2)A spell which allows a wizard to "trap" a door or
	  maybe an object which is like a landmine, when you
	  drop it it becomes a trap. Imagine an object called
	  a hole, you just drop it and you get a trap door
	  (like something from a roadrunner cartoon).

	And a final note, 

			these suggestions are just that.

			suggestions.....


